{
  "about": "physrisk's non-flood hazard grids the asset panel can map, read from the public os-climate-physical-risk bucket. app/engine/hazard_grids.py checks every entry against physrisk's embedded inventory (physrisk/data/static/hazard/inventory.json) and raises if a path or param value is missing. Every non-flood inventory resource is either in layers or in excluded, with a reason. Scenarios and years come from the inventory, never from this file. nodata_values are fill values the arrays use besides NaN and -9999, read as no data. index is the value picked on the array's leading axis (null when the array has only one). feeds_damage is true only for the resources physrisk's damage figures use for this app (Fire, Hail, Wind). Ramps run from the lowest value to the highest, one hue each, and pass the dataviz validator's --ordinal checks (lightness monotone, adjacent steps >= 0.06 apart, light end >= 2:1 on the surface): `node scripts/validate_palette.js \"#86b6ef,#5598e7,#2a78d6,#1c5cab,#0d366b\" --mode light --surface \"#fcfcfb\" --ordinal` and `node scripts/validate_palette.js \"#184f95,#256abf,#3987e5,#6da7ec,#b7d3f6\" --mode dark --surface \"#0d0d0d\" --ordinal`, against the --surface colours in app/front/src/styles.css, both ALL CHECKS PASS (2026-11-13). Re-run them before changing a ramp.",
  "ramps": {
    "light": [
      "#86b6ef",
      "#5598e7",
      "#2a78d6",
      "#1c5cab",
      "#0d366b"
